Z||000000||Spektyr||04-20-2001||01:16 AM||||Well, it don't really get much more Midwest than Kansas, and god knows there isn't much else to do around here than drive somewhere more interesting.<P>Anyone have anything planned around here (within a few hours drive)?<P>Someone want to plan something around here?<P>I'd like to meet up with some people who can give me some good advice on my car, see what they've done with theirs, and generally just hang out with folks who don't think I'm crazy for owning a car that has to be lifted off it's motor for repairs that other cars can do on jackstands.  (I mean the stuff really worth doing usually isn't easy, right?)<P>Also hoping to learn of some local places that don't give me blank stares when I ask for parts for an 85 Fiero.  "Duh... it still runs?"<P>"Yes, it runs.  I know which end of the wrench to point at the bolt, do you?"||||reg||3
Z||000001||GarethWright||04-20-2001||01:39 AM||||Not really in Driving over to hang out distance, but I am in Broken Arrow OK, just outside Tulsa.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spektyr||04-20-2001||01:41 AM||||Yeah, Tulsa isn't exactly 'want to catch a movie' kind of driving distance, but if we could get a dozen or so people together for a 'Show and Tell' kind of thing, then go cruise around a bit, that would be cool.<P>Get a dozen or two Fiero's tooling around together.  We'd get some looks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WhiteWolf||04-20-2001||11:40 AM||||I'm in Dallas.. I might be able to make it to Oklahoma for a gathering....<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000004||stimpy||04-20-2001||03:54 PM||||Well then, start making plans now for Fiero Club of Oklahoma's 9th annual Southwest Regional Firo meet. It will be held at Ferguson Pontiac in Norman on May 19th. Show will start at 10am til 3-4p, then will adjourn to a local park for catered BBQ and BYOB malted beverages. (Real beer from out of state participants greatly envied. Damn low point beer!) After that we will caravan into OKC for a cruise-in at Coit's Root Beer stand (which is always a BLAST!).<BR>Price of entry to the show which includes souvenier t-shirt and the BBQ will be $25. Please email me if you have any questions. This year we are hoping for at least 30 cars, s everyone welcome. Please don't trip if your car isn't "show quality". 95% of our cars are daily drivers.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spektyr||04-21-2001||12:41 AM||||I'll see if I can get that night off (I work 3rd shift) as it would suck to stay up all day, drive to OK, hang out, drive back and then go to work for 10 hrs.<P>My new Fiero seems pretty mechanically sound, and I'll know whether the 2-3hr trip each way is doable by then.  I've flogged the motor pretty good in the last couple days with no complaints.<P>Heck, it practically begs to get up to 5000 rpm.<BR><P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)||||reg||1
